{"type": "text", "content": "Designing Grok Bot for a world of persistent agents"}
{"type": "text", "content": "How we designed Grok Bot for agents that persist beyond a single session — from a chat history to a Bot roster, presence, a computer of the Bot’s own, and work that starts without a prompt."}
{"type": "text", "content": "When we started designing Grok Bot, one of the central questions was how the interface should shape the relationship between user and agent. Most AI interfaces are organized around a chat session the user operates. Each session begins with setup, unfolds as the user looks on, and ends when the conversation stops."}
{"type": "text", "content": "We wanted to design for an agent that persists beyond any one session and can carry responsibility on its own. That meant reconsidering some of the basic objects and signals of the interface, including what belongs in the sidebar, how an agent shows progress, and when its work should become visible."}
{"type": "figure", "img": "https://x.ai/_next/static/media/wallpaper-light-noon.27_hyf9uycov-.png?dpl=b542f0a51fdbb354684e4e23c9b14ce95dbf39f7", "caption": "", "after_para": 3, "hero": false}
